---
import ProsePage from '../../../templates/ProsePage.astro';
import { routePath } from '../../../i18n/routes.ts';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, EDITION_001 } from '../../../config/site.ts';
---

<ProsePage
  locale="en"
  routeKey="companies"
  title="Companies"
  description="Five ways a company can attach itself to twente.dev — and the four things that explicitly cannot be bought."
>
  <p>
    Do you employ a group of people who build technology in Twente, and want to do something with
    that? This page is ordered by what we need most. In-kind support comes before money here — not
    out of principle, but because a room and forty sandwiches make an evening happen and a figure in
    an account does not.
  </p>

  <h2>What you can do</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Host an edition.</strong> A room for {EDITION_001.capacity} people, food and drinks, and
      someone to open the door. This is the contribution that actually makes an edition possible.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Send your people — on work time.</strong> The scarce resource in this region is not money,
      it is time. Freeing up an evening, or counting it as work, is a bigger contribution than most sponsorship
      sums. It also returns more: people talking to peers who do not work for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Let someone tell a story.</strong> Twelve minutes about something you built, fixed or broke.
      Note the order of operations: this goes through the
      <a href={routePath('contribute', 'en')}>open call</a>, on the same terms as everyone else. A
      speaking slot is not part of a sponsorship deal and will not become one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Bring a demo.</strong> Something that works, on a table, that people can stand around and
      ask questions about. No booth, no flyers, no badge scanner.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Give something in kind.</strong> Printing, recording gear, a photographer, coffee, transport.
      Tell us what you already happen to have; it is often exactly what is missing.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    You can back an edition financially, but there is no rate card and no donate button here. That
    is a conversation per edition, and only relevant once there is something to pay for that cannot
    be given in kind. What was and was not paid for goes into the public write-up afterwards.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get for it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Named on the edition page and in the room, and thanked in the write-up afterwards.</li>
    <li>
      Your people in a room with peers from other organisations and other disciplines — the meeting
      that a single-subject meetup by definition cannot produce.
    </li>
    <li>An honest picture of what is going on in the region, from the people doing the work.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you do not buy</h2>
  <p>
    This list is here because otherwise it gets asked anyway, and it is better answered up front
    than halfway through an evening:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No attendee data.</strong> Not the list, not the badges, for anyone.</li>
    <li><strong>No speaking time.</strong> Not even "just a few words at the opening".</li>
    <li><strong>No editorial influence</strong> over what appears on this site or on stage.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>No exclusivity.</strong> You are not the only one in your industry who may take part, and
      that is never offered.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The same rules apply to the organisations closest to this project — named on
    <a href={routePath('about', 'en')}>about</a>. The full agreement, including how we treat other
    communities' existing sponsors, is on <a href={routePath('partners', 'en')}>partners</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What about the company directory?</h2>
  <p>
    There isn't one, and that is a choice. A directory with three entries reads as an abandoned
    site, and whether twente.dev should be a company directory at all is a question better answered
    after the first edition than before it. So this page is about taking part, not about being
    listed.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting started</h2>
  <p>
    The quickest route is the form on <a href={routePath('contribute', 'en')}>contribute</a> — it says
    what we need to know about a room. Prefer plain e-mail? <a
      href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=Company%20contribution`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a
    >, one paragraph is enough.
  </p>
</ProsePage>
